  {
   "id": "concept2",
   "type": "concept",
   "title": {
    "en": "Performance of the full-wave rectifier"
   },
   "body": {
    "en": "With V_m the peak of each half of the secondary: $V_{dc} = 2V_m/\\pi \\approx 0.636V_m$, $I_{dc} = 2I_m/\\pi$ and $I_{rms} = I_m/\\sqrt{2}$. The ripple factor falls to 0.482 and the maximum efficiency rises to 81.2 %. The drawbacks: each diode must withstand a PIV of 2V_m, and the centre-tapped transformer is bulkier (TUF ≈ 0.693)."
   },
   "points": [
    {
     "en": "V_dc = 2V_m/π, I_rms = I_m/√2"
    },
    {
     "en": "Ripple factor 0.482, efficiency 81.2 %"
    },
    {
     "en": "PIV = 2V_m per diode"
    }
   ],
   "narration": {
    "en": "The full-wave rectifier doubles the d.c. output to 2 V m by pi, cuts the ripple factor to 0.482 and doubles the efficiency to 81.2 percent. But each diode must stand 2 V m.",
    "kn": "ಪೂರ್ಣ-ತರಂಗ ದಿಷ್ಟಕಾರಿ ನೇರ ಔಟ್‌ಪುಟ್ ಅನ್ನು 2Vm/π ಗೆ ದ್ವಿಗುಣಗೊಳಿಸುತ್ತದೆ, ತರಂಗಾಂಶ ಅಂಶ 0.482, ದಕ್ಷತೆ 81.2 ಶೇಕಡಾ. ಆದರೆ ಪ್ರತಿ ಡಯೋಡ್ 2Vm ತಡೆಯಬೇಕು."
   },
   "formula": "V_{dc} = \\frac{2V_m}{\\pi},\\quad I_{rms} = \\frac{I_m}{\\sqrt{2}},\\quad r = 0.482,\\quad \\eta_{max} = 81.2\\%"
  },
